<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <Version>1.2.0</Version>
    <PackageId>TokenGuard.Extensions.Anthropic</PackageId>
    <Title>TokenGuard.Extensions.Anthropic</Title>
    <Authors>Svetlozar Stoykov</Authors>
    <Company>Svetlozar Stoykov</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Svetlozar Stoykov</Copyright>
    <Description>Anthropic integration for TokenGuard on .NET 10. Converts prepared TokenGuard messages to Anthropic request parts and lets TokenGuard use Anthropic to summarize older history when context gets tight. Targets net10.0 only.</Description>
    <PackageTags>tokenguard;anthropic;claude;llm;ai;agents;context-management;token-budget;prompt-management;dotnet</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Requires exactly TokenGuard.Core 1.2.0, and Anthropic 12.53.0 or later. The package dependency on TokenGuard.Core is the exact version [1.2.0], so NuGet reports a mismatched Core version at restore.

Behavior changes, with no signature changes: ForAnthropic() sends every text segment of a message as its own text block and every result of a tool message, where it used to send the first of each; it throws InvalidOperationException for a message it cannot represent, for unpaired tool calls and results, and for tool-call arguments that are not a JSON object. InputTokens() returns the total input of the request, including cache creation and cache read tokens, and null when the response carries no usage. From TokenGuard.Core 1.2.0: the default token budget is 40,000 instead of 25,000, and tool-result masking moves its boundary in steps.

This adapter is covered by unit tests only; no run against the Anthropic API has verified it. Known limits: summarization works with the built-in providers only, and a custom summarizer, compaction strategy, or token counter cannot be registered through the builder; one ConversationContext is for one caller at a time, and overlapping calls are detected on a best-effort basis; token estimates leave out request overhead such as tool schemas and undercount pretty-printed JSON by 17% to 30% until the first provider report; one tool result larger than the window cannot be fitted and the prepare returns CompactionInsufficient; the package targets net10.0 only.

Full details: https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
      <PackageReference Include="Anthropic" Version="12.53.0" />
    </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\TokenGuard.Core\TokenGuard.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
